The Curly Message Format marks

Copyright (c) 2026 G.A.W.Group, s.r.o. All rights reserved.


SCOPE

This file covers the name "Curly Message Format" and the marks in this
directory: curly-icon.svg, curly-wordmark.svg and
curly-wordmark-no-tagline.svg.

These are NOT licensed under the MIT License in the root of this repository.
That license covers the specification and the code. The format is open; its
marks are not.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

Refer to the format by name, including saying that your software implements,
supports, reads or writes the Curly Message Format.

Use the marks, unchanged, to refer to the format: in documentation, in an
article, in a list of supported formats, on a slide, in a README. You may
scale them to any size and render them in any single colour, which is what
they are built for.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Change a mark's shape, its proportions or its wording, or combine it with
other elements into a new mark.

Use the name or the marks as the name or the mark of your own project,
product or organisation, or in any way that suggests G.A.W.Group, s.r.o.
endorses you or is affiliated with you, or that your implementation is the
official one.

Sell merchandise carrying the marks.

Register the name or the marks, or anything confusingly similar to them, as a
trademark.


ANYTHING ELSE

If you need something these terms do not cover, open an issue in this
repository and ask.
